Z||000000||juddev||05-12-2000||09:41 PM||||Has any one had this problem, My clutch works fine most of the time but sometimes it lets out completely within 1 inch of the floor. I have done the clutch pedal fix and I have the cast iron clutch fork actuator   {not sure of the term} I think it might be the clutch slave cylinder, but I am not sure. Also has anyone replaced A slave cyl?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiasco||05-13-2000||01:01 AM||||Yeah, I think just about all of us have changed out the slave. (or rebuilt it) One of the joys of owning a Fiero, apparently.<BR>Search the forum- there's loads of posts on clutch hydraulics. "Clutch info. uncovered" is one thread from awhile ago that covers most of it. (it's about 8 million pages long, though, so have fun.) -ignore the part about using ATF- ...no good.<P>Replacing the slave is actually pretty simple, if that is the problem, but read up on how to bleed the system if you haven't- that part can be trickier.<p>[This message has been edited by Fiasco (edited 05-13-2000).]||||reg||2
